# Cursor / Windsurf Global Rules: Architecture Sync

> Level: MANDATORY
> Purpose: Prevent architecture drift and codebase degradation by enforcing Architecture First and Same-Turn Synchronization.

## 1. Architecture First (Human Approval Gate)
- If ARCHITECTURE.md does not exist, OR header status is NOT `✅ Confirmed` / `✅ 確定済`:
  - You MUST propose and generate the 27-section architecture specification and obtain explicit human user approval before writing any implementation code.
  - In headless or non-interactive environments, keep status as `◼ Unconfirmed`, output only the architecture proposal/spec, and DO NOT proceed with implementation code (AI self-approval is strictly forbidden).

## 2. Same-Turn Synchronization
- Whenever you add or alter:
  - Services, modules, or domain slices
  - Database tables, columns, or relations
  - API endpoints, contracts, or webhooks
  - Background workers, queues, or scheduled jobs
  - External third-party integrations
  - Environment variables
  YOU MUST update the architecture document in the exact same response/turn. Zero architectural drift across commits.

## 3. Grounding & Status Symbols
- Every statement must be 100% grounded in code (`file:line`). Missing elements must be marked as `> Not Found`.
- Use the 4 status symbols:
  - `✅` In Code (実装済み: verified by test or manual run)
  - `◼` Planned (設計確定・未実装: boundary agreed, no code yet)
  - `⚠️` Drift / Review (乖離・要確認: discrepancy or refactoring needed)
  - `~~Deprecated~~` (廃止・非推奨)

## 4. Header & Changelog Specification
- Header must include machine-readable marker:
  `<!-- archguard: synced=base-commit-hash status=confirmed date=YYYY-MM-DD -->`
  `> Last Updated: YYYY-MM-DD · Synced Commit: [base-commit-hash] · Status: ✅ Confirmed`
- Append 1 line to §27 Changelog on every structural change:
  `- YYYY-MM-DD · [commit-hash] · <Summary> · Sections: §4, §9`
